@startuml
title T12-WF06 — AI Churn Monitoring Agent (Sequence)
autonumber
participant "Schedule Trigger" as SCHED
participant "n8n WF06\nChurn Monitoring" as N8N
participant "NestJS Backend" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Gemini API" as AI
participant "NestJS CustomerTask API" as CTASK

SCHED -> N8N: Daily scheduled run
activate N8N
N8N -> API: GET active customer cohort
API -> DB: Select active customers
DB --> API: Customer IDs
API --> N8N: Cohort
loop For each customer (bounded batch)
N8N -> API: GET profile, engagement, follow-up and feedback signals
API -> DB: Read customer/activity/follow-up/feedback records
DB --> API: Available facts and data coverage
API --> N8N: Customer signals
N8N -> N8N: Normalize available features and data coverage; do not calculate canonical risk
N8N -> API: POST evaluate churn policy
API -> API: Apply deterministic, versioned backend risk policy
API -> DB: Insert CustomerChurnAssessment history record
DB --> API: Assessment ID + canonical score/level or INSUFFICIENT_DATA
API --> N8N: Canonical assessment + evidence summary
N8N -> AI: Request explanation grounded in canonical score and supplied evidence
AI --> N8N: Explanation (not an authoritative score)
N8N -> N8N: Validate explanation against assessment/evidence
N8N -> API: PATCH/save validated explanation
API -> DB: Update assessment explanation/audit
DB --> API: Updated assessment
API --> N8N: Explanation saved
alt Canonical risk is HIGH/CRITICAL
N8N -> CTASK: POST /api/v1/customer-tasks (canonical) with customerId, assessmentId, dedupe key
CTASK -> DB: Insert/reuse customer_tasks and audit entry
DB --> CTASK: Task ID and status
CTASK --> N8N: Task created/already exists (idempotent)
else LOW/MEDIUM or insufficient evidence
N8N -> N8N: Keep assessment without high-risk escalation
end
end
deactivate N8N
note over N8N,API
NestJS owns the deterministic risk score/level and persistence
to NestJS. n8n normalizes features and requests an assessment; AI only explains
the backend result. `CustomerTask` is the operational task for retention; `ReviewTask` remains reserved for explicit approval/review.
end note
@enduml
